   "id": 510462,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the numbers in base 3 up to 100<sub>3</sub>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>There are three digits in the base three system:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0,1,2.\"></span></p>\n<p>When you run out of digits, you need two digits. Because the place value is 3 in the base 3 system, start with a 1 in the 3s place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"10,11,12\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, add 2 in the 3s place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"20,21,22\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, you have run out of digits in the 3s place. Now, you move over to the <span data-math=\"{3^2}\"></span> place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"100\"></span></p>\n<p>This is where you were told to stop.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0, 1, 2, 10, 11, 12, 20, 21, 22, 100"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
